{"type": "step", "ts": 1793241477.289, "step": "critic", "status": "done", "attempt": 1, "stats": {"model": "nvidia/Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL", "label": "Super VL", "latency_s": 2.39, "tokens_in": 1339, "tokens_out": 449, "cost_usd": 0.000806, "calls": 1}, "data": {"what_happened": "The robot picked up the soda can at t=2.4s, moved it to the place target [0.5, 0.2, 0.2], and released it at t=4.2s with the can's bottom 11.4 cm above the floor. The can then fell and tipped over to 90 degrees by t=5.8s. The images show the can upright in the gripper at t=3.3s, then lying on its side on the floor from t=5.0s onward, while the Rubik's cube remains untouched at [0.5, 0.0, 0.028].", "evidence": "Events: grasped soda_can at t=2.4s; released at t=4.2s center [0.498, 0.182, 0.175], bottom 11.4 cm above floor; tipped over (90 deg) at t=5.8s. Measured failure: soda_can tilted 90 deg (max allowed 20).", "category": "dropped_object", "root_cause": "The release height was 11.4 cm, far above the ~1 cm threshold, so the can was dropped instead of placed. It fell onto the floor and tipped over. The place target z=0.2 was also far above the can's resting height (~0.061 m), so even a gentle set-down would not have occurred at that height.", "suggested_fix": "Lower the place target so the can is set down gently: use xyz [0.444, 0.0, 0.061] (about 4 cm left of the cube's center at x=0.5, y=0.0, on the floor) with the gripper closing to just above the surface, then open and retract. This keeps the can upright and to the left of the Rubik's cube as required."}}
